        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "718d443c-dc47-3679-b442-7c152035b4d2",
                "word": "globuline",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0fcd3807-be6c-4f9e-8e9d-4f519fab0830",
                        "entry_id": "718d443c-dc47-3679-b442-7c152035b4d2",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "globulines"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b4fc2523-5d03-3481-9f78-bbe6cac3d551",
                        "entry_id": "718d443c-dc47-3679-b442-7c152035b4d2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Protéine sérique de plus grande taille, de poids moléculaire plus élevé et plus soluble dans l’eau que l’albumine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab76cffb-b7c1-4849-92ef-f363f3368a13",
                                "sense_id": "b4fc2523-5d03-3481-9f78-bbe6cac3d551",
                                "text": "La globuline est insoluble dans une dissolution saline, contenant de l’albumine, mais elle est soluble dans l’eau pure."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bd7c700-442b-4316-94bf-b579fced26ea",
                                "sense_id": "b4fc2523-5d03-3481-9f78-bbe6cac3d551",
                                "text": "Les globulines sont insolubles dans l'eau, solubles dans une solution de chlorure de sodium à 1 p. 10, précipitée par un excès de chlorure de sodium et par le sulfate de magnésium."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ad7d595-6bc7-4a92-8312-7434165dec0a",
                                "sense_id": "b4fc2523-5d03-3481-9f78-bbe6cac3d551",
                                "text": "Les niveaux d’albumine et de globuline étaient plus élevés dans les variétés de mil chandelle que dans le sorgho, tandis que la quantité de prolamine à structure réticulaire, bêta-prolamine, était plus grande dans le sorgho que dans le mil chandelle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5af827d2-47ff-48e5-a51b-1457b440a368",
                                "sense_id": "b4fc2523-5d03-3481-9f78-bbe6cac3d551",
                                "text": "Les protéines du blanc d’œuf sont réputées pour leurs propriétés foisonnantes (ovalbumine) et stabilisantes de mousse (ovomucine, globuline et lysozyme)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "46e54bdf-ca55-4284-8a2c-b0008ff495a8",
                        "source_entry_id": "718d443c-dc47-3679-b442-7c152035b4d2",
                        "source_sense_id": "b4fc2523-5d03-3481-9f78-bbe6cac3d551",
                        "target_lang_word": "globulin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "globulin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1ff017d-a4f3-38bf-b552-43c5bfa0be7b",
                                        "entry_id": "8c63eded-b8b5-3e73-8510-6233bf8027d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of a group of simple proteins, soluble in water only in the presence of salts, that are coagulated by heat"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc085815-e958-4fae-850a-b2247211d97a",
                                                "sense_id": "d1ff017d-a4f3-38bf-b552-43c5bfa0be7b",
                                                "text": "The most effective approach to delaying and preventing recurrent HBV infection has been high dose immune globulin (anti-HBsIg) perioperatively and postoperatively (table 4)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49492c84-e494-4000-a108-94b0420a8b3e",
                                                "sense_id": "d1ff017d-a4f3-38bf-b552-43c5bfa0be7b",
                                                "text": "On the good news front, the guide reports that a new hepatitis A vaccine, which is now licensed in Europe, should be available in the United States sometime this year. It provides longer protection than the current recommended vaccine -- immune globulin (IG) -- against the hepatitis A virus, which means it does not have to be administered as frequently."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb5962c2-d96e-454b-b88e-3241a966aa08",
                                                "sense_id": "d1ff017d-a4f3-38bf-b552-43c5bfa0be7b",
                                                "text": "Even for the unprotected, those who are exposed can expect 90 percent effectiveness with a course of postexposure prophylaxis that includes hepatitis B immune globulin and initiation of hepatitis B vaccine."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
